[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0916f02f2a122e2e0169f9cc2ca06c81919cfc8c74b1ae9409","text":"Implemented the tscircuit RP2040 breakout in [index.circuit.tsx](/workspace/index.circuit.tsx), with local JLCPCB imports for:\n\n- [RP2040](/workspace/imports/RP2040.tsx)\n- [W25Q32JVSSIQ flash](/workspace/imports/W25Q32JVSSIQ.tsx)\n- [AP2112K_3_3 regulator](/workspace/imports/AP2112K_3_3TRG1.tsx)\n\nThe board includes USB-C, 3.3 V regulation, QSPI flash, 12 MHz crystal, BOOTSEL and RUN buttons, GP25 LED, and two 10-pin 2.54 mm breakout headers. I verified `routingDisabled` is not used.\n\nValidation run:\n- `bun run typecheck`: passed\n- `tsci check netlist index.circuit.tsx`: passed, 0 errors/warnings\n- `tsci check placement index.circuit.tsx`: passed, 0 DRC errors/warnings\n- `tsci build index.circuit.tsx`: generated `dist/index/circuit.json`, but tscircuit reported routing/DRC warnings from the autorouter and imported/builtin component metadata\n- `tsci snapshot --pcb-only`: failed with a Zod invalid input error during PCB SVG generation\n\n**TSCircuit Developer Feedback**\n- Confusing/surprising: `tsci build` exits code 0 and says the circuit passed even while also saying “Build completed with errors,” which makes success/failure ambiguous.\n- Biggest time waste: autorouting/debugging trace output. The netlist was correct, but build still reported many “missing trace” messages, especially for headers and passives.\n- Helpful changes: clearer separation between netlist correctness, routed-copper completeness, and DRC severity; better docs for USB-C built-in pin selectors; a command to print component port names directly.\n- Specific friction: `standard=\"usb_c\"` selectors were not obvious. Generic names like `VBUS`, `D_P`, `D_N`, `GND` did not bind; numbered pins like `.pin18`, `.pin21`, etc. were needed.\n- CLI command that wasted time: `tsci snapshot --pcb-only`; it failed with a raw Zod union error and no component/file context. It should report which element or property caused the invalid input and how to fix it.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null},"threadId":"019df7b6-383b-7321-9f7d-c8bf4d5a7a28","turnId":"019df7b6-384b-7d02-b734-0ee2edaf1932"}}
